This product consumes and references third-party facts and documents:

1. DeepSeek Harness (@deepseek-ai/dsh and related packages)
   Copyright DeepSeek
   License: MIT
   Use: admission semantics, loader/plugin-manager behaviour and public
   documentation are mirrored as executable contracts. No source code is copied;
   the semantics are re-implemented and locked by golden fixtures.

2. dsh.so plugin registry (https://www.dsh.so)
   Data licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   Use: install-verification levels (L1–L5), security tier and download/star
   rankings are consumed as *priors* and are always surfaced with the tier
   `measured-registry` and an attribution to dsh.so. Their conclusions are never
   reworded into stronger claims (e.g. "works on your machine").

3. npm registry (https://registry.npmjs.org)
   Use: package metadata only (version, engines, peerDependencies, deprecation,
   publish time). Tarballs are never redistributed by this project.

4. omdsh-dev/dsh-hub-workshop catalog (dsh-hub-index/v0.4)
   License: MIT (repository)
   Use: hub inclusion status and manifest conventions (read-only).

5. Reference implementations consulted for failure modes and boundaries:
   - lxzy-7/dsh-plugin-guard (MIT) — boot-level health check cannot see a white screen
   - nzl153/dsh-preflight (licence unknown, archived) — static preflight was absorbed upstream
   - LX2000WASD/dsh-web-plugin-manager (archived) — duplicate loader row id breaks boot
   No code from these projects is included. See quarantine/vendor-manifest.json.

This project provides NO security assurance. Malware and supply-chain auditing is
out of scope; see COMPLIANCE.md §5.
